      <div type="clause" n="1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:WlArtRetr">Wl art retr</ref> 1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-lond"><pb n="489–490" ed="#liebermann"/>super omnia unum Deum uellet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.7"/> per totum regnum suum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.8"/> uenerari, unam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.9"/> fidem Christi semper inuiolatam custodiri, pacem et securitatem et concordiam, iudicium et iustitiam inter Anglos et Normannos, similiter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.10"/> inter Francigenos<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.11"/> et Britones<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.d"/> Wallie et Cornubie, et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.7"/> Pictos et Scotos<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.d"/> Albanie, similiter inter Francos et insulicolas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.12"/> omnium insularum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="g" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.g"/> et prouinciarum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.13"/>, que pertinent ad coronam et ad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.7"/> dignitatem et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.14"/> ad defensionem et ad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.7"/> obseruationem et ad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.7"/> honorem regni<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.15"/>, et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.16"/> inter omnes sibi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.17"/> subiectos per uniuersam monarchiam regni Britannie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.a"/> firmiter et inuiolabiliter modis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.1"/> omnibus obseruari, ita quod nullus alii forisfaciat in ullo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.2"/>, super<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.3"/> forisfacturam nostram plenam.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-guildhall"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.5"/><pb n="489–490" ed="#liebermann"/>Imprimis quod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-exchequer"><pb n="489–490" ed="#liebermann"/>Statuimus imprimis</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="1" corresp="#wit-rs"><pb n="244" ed="#robertson"/>Imprimis, quidem super omnia unum Deum vellet p. t. r. s. venerari...pacem et securitatem et concordiam, iudicium et iusticiam, inter Anglos et Normannos, similiter inter Francigenos et Britones Walliae et Cornubiae, et Pictos et Scottos Albaniae, similiter inter Francos et insulicolas omnium insularum et provinciarum et patriarum quae pertinent ad coronam et ad dignitatem et ad defensionem et ad observationem et ad honorem regni, et inter omnes sibi subiectos per universam monarchiam regni Britanniae firmiter et inviolabiliter modis omnibus observari, ita quod nullus alii forisfaciat in ullo super forisfacturam nostram plenam.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-rs"><pb n="245" ed="#robertson"/>In the first place he desires above all that one God should be honoured throughout the whole of his kingdom,...and that peace, security and concord, law and justice should be observed by all means, firmly and inviolably, among English and Normans, likewise among those of French birth and the Britons of Wales and Cornwall, and the Picts and Scots of Albania, and likewise among the French and the inhabitants of all the islands, provinces and countries which appertain to the Crown and to the dignity, defence, maintenance and honour of the realm, and among all his subjects throughout the whole realm of Britain, so that no-one shall do any injury to another in any respect, under pain of incurring the full fine for insubordination to us.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="489, 490"><ref target="clause:WlArt_1">Wl art 1</ref>; <ref target="clause:WlArtRetr_9">Wl art retr 9</ref>; <ref target="clause:WlArt_9">Wl art 9f.</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 1 | vgl. u. 9 | Wl art. 9 f.</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:WlArtRetr_9">Wl art retr 9</ref>; <ref target="clause:WlArtRetr_11">Wl art retr 11</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 244–245 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text added from Gesetze I p. 489–490, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Dies Stück ist nur ein Theil der</hi> Leges Angl. s. XIII in. Londoniis coll., <hi rend="italic">ed. Liebermann p.</hi> 32</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This piece is only a part of the Leges Angl. s. XIII in. Londoniis coll., ed. Liebermann p. 32</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">note marker not found in the text</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">das aus</hi> Wl art. <hi rend="italic">entnommene ist kleiner gedruckt.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">what is taken from Wl art. is printed in smaller type.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">note marker not found in the text</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Verf. will durchweg England als identisch mit Grossbritannien darstellen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the author consistently seeks to present England as identical with Great Britain</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.e" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Wl art. 4{31}; <hi rend="italic">u.</hi> 17{64}</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. Wl art. 4{31}; below 17{64}</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">note marker not found in the text</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.f" n="f" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Verdrehung des Textes zur Freibriefform</hi> (<hi rend="italic">vgl. u.</hi> 17{66}), <hi rend="italic">von</hi> K3 <hi rend="italic">noch fortgesetzt. Den Pluralis majestatis setzt auch die Classe</hi> Ra Vi <hi rend="italic">zu</hi> Art. Wl Inscr.{1} <hi rend="italic">ein</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">distortion of the text into the form of a charter of liberties (cf. below 17{66}), carried further still by K3. The class Ra Vi likewise introduces the plural of majesty at Art. Wl Inscr.{1}</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">note marker not found in the text</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.g" n="g" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ähnliche Phrasen setzt Verf. zu</hi> ECf. 11, 1 A 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the author adds similar phrases at ECf. 11, 1 A 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Carta — etc. <hi rend="italic">Sc, Nachtrag</hi> 14. <hi rend="italic">Jh.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Carta — etc. Sc, 14th-cent. addition</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">note marker not found in the text</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">Dei gratia</hi> <hi rend="italic">fügt zu K3</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">K3 adds <hi rend="italic">Dei gratia</hi></seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">note marker not found in the text</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-cie et Anglie <hi rend="italic">Se</hi>(<hi rend="italic">lden</hi> Eadmeri Hist. Novor. 189 [<hi rend="italic">aus</hi> K3?])</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-cie et Anglie Se(lden Eadmeri Hist. Novor. 189 [from K3?])</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">note marker not found in the text</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Anglicis <hi rend="italic">K3</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Anglicis K3</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">note marker not found in the text</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Überschriften erfindet</hi> (<hi rend="italic">laut p.</hi> 194) <hi rend="italic">Se, hier fortgelassen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Se invents headings (according to p. 194); omitted here</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">note marker not found in the text</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">quid <hi rend="italic">Co;</hi> quidem <hi rend="italic">Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">quid Co; quidem Or</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">note marker not found in the text</note></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Sc Hg K3</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">omitted in Sc Hg K3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nostrum <hi rend="italic">Sc Hg K3</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nostrum Sc Hg K3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">unamque <hi rend="italic">Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">unamque Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="WlArtRetr_1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">489</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">s. i. <hi rend="italic">fehlt Sc K3</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s. i. omitted in Sc K3</seg></note>
